ren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_(cropped2).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg/120px-Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg/250px-Darren_Bailey_at_a_2022_Campaign_Event_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"364\" data-file-height=\"485\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JB_Pritzker\" title=\"JB Pritzker\">JB Pritzker</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey\" title=\"Darren Bailey\">Darren Bailey</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Mitchell\" title=\"Christian Mitchell\">Christian Mitchell</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Aaron Del Mar</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Illinois\" title=\"Governor of Illinois\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JB_Pritzker\" title=\"JB Pritzker\">JB Pritzker</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1758\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCvU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Ifexist not redirect\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ifexist_not_redirect\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Illinois gubernatorial election\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"{{Main|2026 Illinois gubernatorial election}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1759\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1758\" id=\"mwCvY\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Illinois_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Illinois gubernatorial election\">2026 Illinois gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwCvc\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JB_Pritzker\" title=\"JB Pritzker\" id=\"mwCvg\">JB Pritzker</a>, a Democrat, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Illinois_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Illinois gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwCvk\">2022</a> with 54.9% of the vote and is running for a third term.<sup about=\"#mwt1762\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-IL2026_34-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"IL2026\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IL2026-34\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-IL2026-34\" id=\"mwCvo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCvs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCvw\">[</span>31<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCv0\">]</span></span></a></sup> With Lieutenant Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juliana_Stratton\" title=\"Juliana Stratton\" id=\"mwCv4\">Juliana Stratton</a> seeking Illinois's U.S. Senate seat in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_election_in_Illinois\" title=\"2026 United States Senate election in Illinois\" id=\"mwCv8\">2026</a>, Pritzker's running mate is former state representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Mitchell\" title=\"Christian Mitchell\" id=\"mwCwA\">Christian Mitchell</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1765\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-161\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-161\" id=\"mwCwE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCwI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwM\">[</span>151<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Pritzker won the Democratic nomination unopposed.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwCwU\">On the Republican side, former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois_Senate\" title=\"Illinois Senate\" id=\"mwCwY\">state senator</a> and 2022 Republican nominee for governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darren_Bailey\" title=\"Darren Bailey\" id=\"mwCwc\">Darren Bailey</a> secured the nomination against former vice president of policy for the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois_Policy_Institute\" title=\"Illinois Policy Institute\" id=\"mwCwg\">Illinois Policy Institute</a> Ted Dabrowski, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DuPage_County,_Illinois\" title=\"DuPage County, Illinois\" id=\"mwCwk\">DuPage County</a> Sheriff James Mendrick, and real estate developer Rick Heidner.<sup about=\"#mwt1766\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-IL2026_34-3\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"IL2026\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-IL2026-34\" id=\"mwCwo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCws\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCww\">[</span>31<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCw0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1767\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCw4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"25\" id=\"mwCw8\" aria-labelledby=\"Iowa\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Iowa\">Iowa</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Iowa\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1768\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCxA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Iowa gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Iowa\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Iowa gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Iowa gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Zach Lahn IA State Fair 2026.jog (cropped).jpg\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"150x150px\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"Zach Lahn\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Derek Wulf]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Rob Sand campaign headshot (cropped 2).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Rob Sand]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Dave Muhlbauer\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Iowa|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kim Reynolds]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1769\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1770\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1771\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1768\" id=\"mwCxE\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Iowa gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iowa.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Flag_of_Iowa.svg/60px-Flag_of_Iowa.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Flag_of_Iowa.svg/120px-Flag_of_Iowa.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"714\" data-file-height=\"477\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Iowa_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Iowa gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Zach_Lahn_IA_State_Fair_2026.jog_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"286\" data-file-height=\"409\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"105\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_(cropped_2).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_(cropped_2).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/120px-Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/250px-Rob_Sand_campaign_headshot_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1128\" data-file-height=\"1503\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Zach Lahn</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rob_Sand\" title=\"Rob Sand\">Rob Sand</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derek_Wulf\" title=\"Derek Wulf\">Derek Wulf</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Dave Muhlbauer</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Iowa\" title=\"Governor of Iowa\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Reynolds\" title=\"Kim Reynolds\">Kim Reynolds</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1772\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCxI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Ifexist not redirect\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ifexist_not_redirect\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Iowa gubernatorial election\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"{{Main|2026 Iowa gubernatorial election}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1773\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1772\" id=\"mwCxM\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iowa_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Iowa gubernatorial election\">2026 Iowa gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwCxQ\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Reynolds\" title=\"Kim Reynolds\" id=\"mwCxU\">Kim Reynolds</a>, a Republican, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Iowa_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Iowa gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwCxY\">2022</a> with 58.1% of the vote. While she is eligible to run for re-election to a third full term, she has decided not to run.<sup about=\"#mwt1776\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-162\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-162\" id=\"mwCxc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCxg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxk\">[</span>152<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwCxs\">Republican candidates included state representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Andrews_(American_politician)\" title=\"Eddie Andrews (American politician)\" id=\"mwCxw\">Eddie Andrews</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1779\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-AndrewsIA_163-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"AndrewsIA\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AndrewsIA-163\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-AndrewsIA-163\" id=\"mwCx0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCx4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCx8\">[</span>153<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyA\">]</span></span></a></sup> U.S. Representative for Iowa's 4th congressional district <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randy_Feenstra\" title=\"Randy Feenstra\" id=\"mwCyE\">Randy Feenstra</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1782\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CBSNews1_164-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CBSNews1\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBSNews1-164\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CBSNews1-164\" id=\"mwCyI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCyM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyQ\">[</span>154<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyU\">]</span></span></a></sup> former director of the Iowa Department of Administrative Services Adam Steen,<sup about=\"#mwt1785\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Steen_165-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Steen\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Steen-165\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Steen-165\" id=\"mwCyY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCyc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyg\">[</span>155<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyk\">]</span></span></a></sup> businessman Zach Lahn,<sup about=\"#mwt1788\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-166\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-166\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-166\" id=\"mwCyo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCys\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyw\">[</span>156<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCy0\">]</span></span></a></sup> and former state representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Sherman_(Iowa_politician)\" title=\"Brad Sherman (Iowa politician)\" id=\"mwCy4\">Brad Sherman</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1791\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-ShermanIA_167-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"ShermanIA\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ShermanIA-167\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-ShermanIA-167\" id=\"mwCy8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCzA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzE\">[</span>157<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzI\">]</span></span></a></sup> Zach Lahn won the nomination on June 2, in what was considered a major upset.<sup about=\"#mwt1794\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-168\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-168\" id=\"mwCzM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCzQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzU\">[</span>158<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwCzc\">On the Democratic side, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Auditor_of_Iowa\" title=\"State Auditor of Iowa\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCzg\">State Auditor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rob_Sand\" title=\"Rob Sand\" id=\"mwCzk\">Rob Sand</a> declared his candidacy in May 2025 and won the nomination as the only candidate to file by the deadline. He is also the only <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iowa_Democratic_Party\" title=\"Iowa Democratic Party\" id=\"mwCzo\">Democratic</a> statewide officeholder in Iowa.<sup about=\"#mwt1797\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SandIA_169-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"SandIA\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-SandIA-169\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-SandIA-169\" id=\"mwCzs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCzw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCz0\">[</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCz4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1798\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCz8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"26\" id=\"mwC0A\" aria-labelledby=\"Kansas\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Kansas\">Kansas</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: Kansas\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1799\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC0E\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Kansas gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Kansas\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Kansas gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Kansas gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Cindy 2 cropped.jpg\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"150x150px\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Cindy Holscher]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[KC Ohaebosim]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"TY mASTERSON (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Ty Masterson]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jeff Klemp]]\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Kansas|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Laura Kelly]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1800\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1801\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1802\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1799\" id=\"mwC0I\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Kansas gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kansas.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Flag_of_Kansas.svg/60px-Flag_of_Kansas.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Flag_of_Kansas.svg/120px-Flag_of_Kansas.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"500\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Kansas_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Kansas gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cindy_2_cropped.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cindy_2_cropped.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cindy_2_cropped.jpg/120px-Cindy_2_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cindy_2_cropped.jpg/250px-Cindy_2_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2233\" data-file-height=\"3225\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"104\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TY_mASTERSON_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TY_mASTERSON_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"614\" data-file-height=\"864\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"106\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cindy_Holscher\" title=\"Cindy Holscher\">Cindy Holscher</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson\" title=\"Ty Masterson\">Ty Masterson</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KC_Ohaebosim\" title=\"KC Ohaebosim\">KC Ohaebosim</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Klemp\" title=\"Jeff Klemp\">Jeff Klemp</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Kansas\" title=\"Governor of Kansas\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Kelly\" title=\"Laura Kelly\">Laura Kelly</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1803\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC0M\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Ifexist not redirect\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ifexist_not_redirect\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Kansas gubernatorial election\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"{{Main|2026 Kansas gubernatorial election}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1804\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1803\" id=\"mwC0Q\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Kansas_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Kansas gubernatorial election\">2026 Kansas gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwC0U\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Kelly\" title=\"Laura Kelly\" id=\"mwC0Y\">Laura Kelly</a>, a Democrat, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Kansas_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Kansas gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC0c\">2022</a> with 49.5% of the vote. She will be term limited  by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kansas_Constitution\" title=\"Kansas Constitution\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC0g\">Kansas Constitution</a> and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwC0k\">State senators <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethan_Corson\" title=\"Ethan Corson\" id=\"mwC0o\">Ethan Corson</a><sup about=\"#mwt1807\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Corson_170-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Corson\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corson-170\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Corson-170\" id=\"mwC0s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC0w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC00\">[</span>160<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC04\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cindy_Holscher\" title=\"Cindy Holscher\" id=\"mwC08\">Cindy Holscher</a><sup about=\"#mwt1810\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Holscher_39-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Holscher\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Holscher-39\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Holscher-39\" id=\"mwC1A\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC1E\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1I\">[</span>35<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1M\">]</span></span></a></sup> ran for the Democratic nomination, with Corson receiving Governor Kelly's endorsement.<sup about=\"#mwt1813\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-171\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-171\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-171\" id=\"mwC1Q\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC1U\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1Y\">[</span>161<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1c\">]</span></span></a></sup> Holscher defeated Corson with 48.8% of the vote on August 4. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwC1g\">Candidates for the Republican nomination included State Senate President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson\" title=\"Ty Masterson\" id=\"mwC1k\">Ty Masterson</a>, Kansas Insurance Commissioner <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicki_Schmidt\" title=\"Vicki Schmidt\" id=\"mwC1o\">Vicki Schmidt</a>, Kansas Secretary of State <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Schwab\" title=\"Scott Schwab\" id=\"mwC1s\">Scott Schwab</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnson_County,_Kansas\" title=\"Johnson County, Kansas\" id=\"mwC1w\">Johnson County</a> Commissioner <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte_O'Hara\" title=\"Charlotte O'Hara\" id=\"mwC10\">Charlotte O'Hara</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1816\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Collyer_172-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Collyer\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Collyer-172\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Collyer-172\" id=\"mwC14\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC18\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2A\">[</span>162<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2E\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1819\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Schwab_173-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Schwab\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Schwab-173\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Schwab-173\" id=\"mwC2I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC2M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2Q\">[</span>163<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2U\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1822\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-O'Hara_174-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"O&apos;Hara\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-O&apos;Hara-174\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-O'Hara-174\" id=\"mwC2Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC2c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2g\">[</span>164<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2k\">]</span></span></a></sup> Masterson won the Republican nomination on August 4 with 43.2% of the vote.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1823\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC2o\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"27\" id=\"mwC2s\" aria-labelledby=\"Maine\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Maine\">Maine</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27\" title=\"Edit section: Maine\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1824\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC2w\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Maine gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Maine\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Maine gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Maine gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Headshot of Hannah Pingree in February 2026 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Hannah Pingree]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Robert Charles (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Robert B. Charles]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image3\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee3\":{\"wt\":\"[[Rick Bennett (Maine politician)|Rick Bennett]]\"},\"party3\":{\"wt\":\"Independent\"},\"popular_vote3\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage3\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Maine|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Janet Mills]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1825\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1826\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1827\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1824\" id=\"mwC20\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Maine gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Maine.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Flag_of_Maine.svg/60px-Flag_of_Maine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Flag_of_Maine.svg/120px-Flag_of_Maine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"6336\" data-file-height=\"4992\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"39\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Maine_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Maine gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Headshot_of_Hannah_Pingree_in_February_2026_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1653\" data-file-height=\"2074\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"108\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Charles_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Charles_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Robert_Charles_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Robert_Charles_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Robert_Charles_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Robert_Charles_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1380\" data-file-height=\"1841\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hannah_Pingree\" title=\"Hannah Pingree\">Hannah Pingree</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_B._Charles\" title=\"Robert B. Charles\">Robert B. Charles</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Bennett_(Maine_politician)\" title=\"Rick Bennett (Maine politician)\">Rick Bennett</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Maine\" title=\"Governor of Maine\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Mills\" title=\"Janet Mills\">Janet Mills</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1828\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC24\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Ifexist not redirect\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ifexist_not_redirect\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Maine gubernatorial election\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"{{Main|2026 Maine gubernatorial election}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1829\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1828\" id=\"mwC28\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Maine_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Maine gubernatorial election\">2026 Maine gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwC3A\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Mills\" title=\"Janet Mills\" id=\"mwC3E\">Janet Mills</a>, a Democrat, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Maine_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Maine gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC3I\">2022</a> with 55.4% of the vote. She will be term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maine_Constitution\" title=\"Maine Constitution\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC3M\">Maine Constitution</a>, and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwC3Q\">Former State House Speaker <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hannah_Pingree\" title=\"Hannah Pingree\" id=\"mwC3U\">Hannah Pingree</a>, the daughter of U.S. Representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chellie_Pingree\" title=\"Chellie Pingree\" id=\"mwC3Y\">Chellie Pingree</a><sup about=\"#mwt1832\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Pingree_175-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Pingree\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pingree-175\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Pingree-175\" id=\"mwC3c\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC3g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3k\">[</span>165<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3o\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated a crowded Democratic field, which included Secretary of State <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shenna_Bellows\" title=\"Shenna Bellows\" id=\"mwC3s\">Shenna Bellows</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1835\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Bellows_176-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Bellows\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bellows-176\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Bellows-176\" id=\"mwC3w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC30\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC34\">[</span>166<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC38\">]</span></span></a></sup> former State Senate President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Jackson\" title=\"Troy Jackson\" id=\"mwC4A\">Troy Jackson</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1838\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TroyDale_177-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"TroyDale\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TroyDale-177\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-TroyDale-177\" id=\"mwC4E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC4I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4M\">[</span>167<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> businessman <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angus_King_III\" title=\"Angus King III\" id=\"mwC4U\">Angus King III</a>, the son of independent U.S. Senator and former Maine governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angus_King\" title=\"Angus King\" id=\"mwC4Y\">Angus King</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1841\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-AngusIII_178-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"AngusIII\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AngusIII-178\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-AngusIII-178\" id=\"mwC4c\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC4g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4k\">[</span>168<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4o\">]</span></span></a></sup> and former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centers_for_Disease_Control_and_Prevention\" title=\"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\" id=\"mwC4s\">Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</a> principal deputy director <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nirav_D._Shah\" title=\"Nirav D. Shah\" id=\"mwC4w\">Dr. Nirav Shah</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1844\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-ShahME_179-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"ShahME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ShahME-179\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-ShahME-179\" id=\"mwC40\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC44\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC48\">[</span>169<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwC5E\">On the Republican side, former U.S. Assistant Secretary of State <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_B._Charles\" title=\"Robert B. Charles\" id=\"mwC5I\">Robert Charles</a><sup about=\"#mwt1847\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CharlesME_180-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CharlesME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CharlesME-180\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CharlesME-180\" id=\"mwC5M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC5Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5U\">[</span>170<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5Y\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated a field which included healthcare executive and member of the Bush family <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_S._Bush\" title=\"Jonathan S. Bush\" id=\"mwC5c\">Jonathan Bush</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1850\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BushME_181-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BushME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BushME-181\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BushME-181\" id=\"mwC5g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC5k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5o\">[</span>171<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5s\">]</span></span></a></sup> real estate businessman David Jones;<sup about=\"#mwt1853\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JonesME_182-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JonesME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JonesME-182\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JonesME-182\" id=\"mwC5w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC50\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC54\">[</span>172<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC58\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maine_Senate\" title=\"Maine Senate\" id=\"mwC6A\">state senator</a> and candidate for governor in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_Maine_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2002 Maine gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC6E\">2002</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Libby\" title=\"James Libby\" id=\"mwC6I\">James Libby</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1856\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-LibbyME_183-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"LibbyME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-LibbyME-183\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-LibbyME-183\" id=\"mwC6M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC6Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6U\">[</span>173<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6Y\">]</span></span></a></sup> former Maine Senate majority leader and candidate for governor in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Maine_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Maine gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC6c\">2018</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garrett_Mason\" title=\"Garrett Mason\" id=\"mwC6g\">Garrett Mason</a>;<sup about=\"#mwt1859\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MasonME_184-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MasonME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MasonME-184\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MasonME-184\" id=\"mwC6k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC6o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6s\">[</span>174<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6w\">]</span></span></a></sup> entrepreneur Owen McCarthy;<sup about=\"#mwt1862\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-McCarthyME_185-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"McCarthyME\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-McCarthyME-185\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-McCarthyME-185\" id=\"mwC60\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC64\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC68\">[</span>175<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7A\">]</span></span></a></sup> businessman Ben Midgley;<sup about=\"#mwt1865\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Midgley_186-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Midgley\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Midgley-186\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Midgley-186\" id=\"mwC7E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC7I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7M\">[</span>176<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> and former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris,_Maine\" title=\"Paris, Maine\" id=\"mwC7U\">Paris</a> selectman Robert Wessels.<sup about=\"#mwt1868\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Wessels_187-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Wessels\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wessels-187\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Wessels-187\" id=\"mwC7Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC7c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7g\">[</span>177<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7k\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwC7o\">Pingree and Charles will be joined on the ballot by independent state senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rick_Bennett_(politician)\" title=\"Rick Bennett (politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC7s\">Rick Bennett</a>, who left the Republican Party shortly before launching his campaign.<sup about=\"#mwt1871\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BennettMaine_41-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BennettMaine\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BennettMaine-41\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BennettMaine-41\" id=\"mwC7w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC70\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC74\">[</span>37<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC78\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1872\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC8A\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"28\" id=\"mwC8E\" aria-labelledby=\"Maryland\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Maryland\">Maryland</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28\" title=\"Edit section: Maryland\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1873\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC8I\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Maryland gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Maryland\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Maryland gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Maryland gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"File:Governor Kuroiwa and Japanese Delegation (cropped2).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Wes Moore]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Aruna Miller]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Dan Cox Mar2020 (49617550556).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Dan Cox]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Robert Krop\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Maryland|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Wes Moore]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1874\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1875\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1876\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1873\" id=\"mwC8M\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Maryland gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Maryland.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_Maryland.svg/60px-Flag_of_Maryland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_Maryland.svg/120px-Flag_of_Maryland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Maryland_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Maryland gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_(cropped2).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_(cropped2).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_%28cropped2%29.jpg/120px-Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_%28cropped2%29.jpg/250px-Governor_Kuroiwa_and_Japanese_Delegation_%28cropped2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2117\" data-file-height=\"2558\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Dan_Cox_Mar2020_(49617550556).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Dan_Cox_Mar2020_(49617550556).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Dan_Cox_Mar2020_%2849617550556%29.jpg/120px-Dan_Cox_Mar2020_%2849617550556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Dan_Cox_Mar2020_%2849617550556%29.jpg/250px-Dan_Cox_Mar2020_%2849617550556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"705\" data-file-height=\"940\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wes_Moore\" title=\"Wes Moore\">Wes Moore</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Cox\" title=\"Dan Cox\">Dan Cox</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aruna_Miller\" title=\"Aruna Miller\">Aruna Miller</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Robert Krop</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Maryland\" title=\"Governor of Maryland\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wes_Moore\" title=\"Wes Moore\">Wes Moore</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1877\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC8Q\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Ifexist not redirect\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ifexist_not_redirect\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Maryland gubernatorial election\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"{{Main|2026 Maryland gubernatorial election}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1878\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1877\" id=\"mwC8U\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Maryland_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Maryland gubernatorial election\">2026 Maryland gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwC8Y\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wes_Moore\" title=\"Wes Moore\" id=\"mwC8c\">Wes Moore</a>, a Democrat, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Maryland_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Maryland gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC8g\">2022</a> with 64.5% of the vote. He is running for re-election to a second term.<sup about=\"#mwt1881\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MooreMD_188-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MooreMD\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MooreMD-188\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MooreMD-188\" id=\"mwC8k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC8o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8s\">[</span>178<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8w\">]</span></span></a></sup> Moore easily defeated physician Eric Felber in the Democratic primary.<sup about=\"#mwt1884\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-189\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-189\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-189\" id=\"mwC80\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC84\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC88\">[</span>179<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwC9E\">A number of Republicans are vying for the party's nomination: businessman Carl Brunner,<sup about=\"#mwt1887\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MD2024_190-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MD2024\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MD2024-190\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MD2024-190\" id=\"mwC9I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC9M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9Q\">[</span>180<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9U\">]</span></span></a></sup> former state delegate and 2022 nominee <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Cox\" title=\"Dan Cox\" id=\"mwC9Y\">Dan Cox</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1890\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CoxMD_191-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CoxMD\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CoxMD-191\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CoxMD-191\" id=\"mwC9c\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC9g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9k\">[</span>181<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9o\">]</span></span></a></sup> businessman <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_Hale_(businessman)\" title=\"Ed Hale (businessman)\" id=\"mwC9s\">Ed Hale</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1893\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HaleGOPMD_192-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"HaleGOPMD\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HaleGOPMD-192\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-HaleGOPMD-192\" id=\"mwC9w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC90\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC94\">[</span>182<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC98\">]</span></span></a></sup> and John Myrick, a candidate for U.S. Senate in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Maryland\" id=\"mwC-A\">2024</a>, have announced their candidacies for governor.<sup about=\"#mwt1896\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-193\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-193\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-193\" id=\"mwC-E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC-I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-M\">[</span>183<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> Cox became the Republican nominee on June 23.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1897\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC-U\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"29\" id=\"mwC-Y\" aria-labelledby=\"Massachusetts\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Massachusetts\">Massachusetts</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=29\" title=\"Edit section: Massachusetts\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1898\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC-c\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Massachusetts gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Massachusetts\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Maura Healey, official portrait, governor (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Maura Healey]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kim Driscoll]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"Michael Minogue\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Shawn Oliver\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Massachusetts|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Maura Healey]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1899\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1900\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1901\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1898\" id=\"mwC-g\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Massachusetts gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg/60px-Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg/120px-Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1500\" data-file-height=\"900\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Massachusetts_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Maura_Healey,_official_portrait,_governor_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Maura_Healey,_official_portrait,_governor_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Maura_Healey%2C_official_portrait%2C_governor_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Maura_Healey%2C_official_portrait%2C_governor_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Maura_Healey%2C_official_portrait%2C_governor_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Maura_Healey%2C_official_portrait%2C_governor_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2994\" data-file-height=\"3879\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"116\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maura_Healey\" title=\"Maura Healey\">Maura Healey</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Michael Minogue</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Driscoll\" title=\"Kim Driscoll\">Kim Driscoll</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Shawn Oliver</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Massachusetts\" title=\"Governor of Massachusetts\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maura_Healey\" title=\"Maura Healey\">Maura Healey</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1902\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC-k\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1903\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1902\" id=\"mwC-o\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Massachusetts_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\">2026 Massachusetts gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwC-s\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maura_Healey\" title=\"Maura Healey\" id=\"mwC-w\">Maura Healey</a>, a Democrat, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Massachusetts_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Massachusetts gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwC-0\">2022</a> with 63.7% of the vote. Healey is running for re-election for a second term in office.<sup about=\"#mwt1904\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MauraHealey_44-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MauraHealey\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MauraHealey-44\" id=\"mwC-4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_A\">[</span>40<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_E\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwC_I\">On the Republican side, businessman Mike Minogue defeated former chief administrator and acting general manager of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massachusetts_Bay_Transportation_Authority\" title=\"Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority\" id=\"mwC_M\">Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority</a> Brian Shortsleeve<sup about=\"#mwt1907\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Shortsleeve_194-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Shortsleeve\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Shortsleeve-194\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Shortsleeve-194\" id=\"mwC_Q\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC_U\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_Y\">[</span>184<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_c\">]</span></span></a></sup> on September 1, 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt1908\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Minogue_46-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Minogue\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Minogue-46\" id=\"mwC_g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC_k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_o\">[</span>42<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_s\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1909\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC_w\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"30\" id=\"mwC_0\" aria-labelledby=\"Michigan\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Michigan\">Michigan</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=30\" title=\"Edit section: Michigan\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1910\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC_4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Michigan gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Michigan\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Michigan gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Michigan gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"SOS Jocelyn Benson web (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jocelyn Benson]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Winnie Brinks]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Rep. John James official photo, 118th Congress (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[John James (Michigan politician)|John James]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jay DeBoyer]]\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Michigan|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Gretchen Whitmer]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1911\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1912\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1913\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1910\" id=\"mwC_8\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Michigan gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Michigan.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Flag_of_Michigan.svg/60px-Flag_of_Michigan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Flag_of_Michigan.svg/120px-Flag_of_Michigan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"342\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Michigan_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Michigan gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1895\" data-file-height=\"2336\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"110\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rep._John_James_official_photo,_118th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rep._John_James_official_photo,_118th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Rep._John_James_official_photo%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Rep._John_James_official_photo%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Rep._John_James_official_photo%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Rep._John_James_official_photo%2C_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"441\" data-file-height=\"547\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"110\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson\" title=\"Jocelyn Benson\">Jocelyn Benson</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_James_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"John James (Michigan politician)\">John James</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winnie_Brinks\" title=\"Winnie Brinks\">Winnie Brinks</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_DeBoyer\" title=\"Jay DeBoyer\">Jay DeBoyer</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Michigan\" title=\"Governor of Michigan\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gretchen_Whitmer\" title=\"Gretchen Whitmer\">Gretchen Whitmer</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1914\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDAA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Michigan gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1915\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1914\" id=\"mwDAE\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Michigan_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Michigan gubernatorial election\">2026 Michigan gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDAI\">Democratic Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gretchen_Whitmer\" title=\"Gretchen Whitmer\" id=\"mwDAM\">Gretchen Whitmer</a> was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Michigan_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Michigan gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDAQ\">2022</a> with 54.5% of the vote. She is term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Michigan\" title=\"Constitution of Michigan\" id=\"mwDAU\">Michigan Constitution</a> in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDAY\">Secretary of State <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson\" title=\"Jocelyn Benson\" id=\"mwDAc\">Jocelyn Benson</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genessee_County,_Michigan\" title=\"Genessee County, Michigan\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDAg\">Genessee County</a> Sheriff Chris Swanson announced campaigns for the Democratic nomination.<sup about=\"#mwt1918\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Benson_195-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Benson\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Benson-195\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Benson-195\" id=\"mwDAk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDAo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDAs\">[</span>185<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDAw\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1921\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Swanson_196-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Swanson\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Swanson-196\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Swanson-196\" id=\"mwDA0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDA4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDA8\">[</span>186<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDBA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Benson easily defeated Swanson with 83.2% of the vote on August 4 and became the Democratic nominee.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDBE\">Businessman, 2022 candidate for governor and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election\" title=\"2024 United States presidential election\" id=\"mwDBI\">2024 candidate for president</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perry_Johnson_(businessman)\" title=\"Perry Johnson (businessman)\" id=\"mwDBM\">Perry Johnson</a>; and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"United States House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDBQ\">U.S. Representative</a> for Michigan's 10th congressional district and nominee for U.S. Senate in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Michigan\" id=\"mwDBU\">2018</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"2020 United States Senate election in Michigan\" id=\"mwDBY\">2020</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_James_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"John James (Michigan politician)\" id=\"mwDBc\">John James</a> announced bids for the Republican nomination.<sup about=\"#mwt1924\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JamesMI_197-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JamesMI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JamesMI-197\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JamesMI-197\" id=\"mwDBg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDBk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDBo\">[</span>187<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDBs\">]</span></span></a></sup> James defeated Johnson with 50.1% of the vote on August 4.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDBw\">Detroit mayor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Duggan\" title=\"Mike Duggan\" id=\"mwDB0\">Mike Duggan</a>, a former Democrat, announced his intention to run for governor as an independent in December 2024.<sup about=\"#mwt1927\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Duggan_198-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Duggan\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Duggan-198\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Duggan-198\" id=\"mwDB4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDB8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCA\">[</span>188<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCE\">]</span></span></a></sup> He suspended his campaign in May 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt1930\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-199\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-199\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-199\" id=\"mwDCI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDCM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCQ\">[</span>189<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1931\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDCY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"31\" id=\"mwDCc\" aria-labelledby=\"Minnesota\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Minnesota\">Minnesota</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31\" title=\"Edit section: Minnesota\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1932\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDCg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Minnesota gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Minnesota\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Minnesota gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Minnesota gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Artemis II Klobuchar (3x4 cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Amy Klobuchar]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"Ben Schierer\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Lisa Demuth, 2026 (3x4).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Lisa Demuth]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Ryan Wilson\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Minnesota|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Tim Walz]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1933\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1934\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1935\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1932\" id=\"mwDCk\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Minnesota gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Minnesota.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Flag_of_Minnesota.svg/60px-Flag_of_Minnesota.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Flag_of_Minnesota.svg/120px-Flag_of_Minnesota.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"600\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Minnesota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Minnesota gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0055AA;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Artemis_II_Klobuchar_(3x4_cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Artemis_II_Klobuchar_(3x4_cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Artemis_II_Klobuchar_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/120px-Artemis_II_Klobuchar_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Artemis_II_Klobuchar_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/250px-Artemis_II_Klobuchar_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1257\" data-file-height=\"1674\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Lisa_Demuth,_2026_(3x4).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Lisa_Demuth,_2026_(3x4).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Lisa_Demuth%2C_2026_%283x4%29.jpg/120px-Lisa_Demuth%2C_2026_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Lisa_Demuth%2C_2026_%283x4%29.jpg/250px-Lisa_Demuth%2C_2026_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1215\" data-file-height=\"1620\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Klobuchar\" title=\"Amy Klobuchar\">Amy Klobuchar</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisa_Demuth\" title=\"Lisa Demuth\">Lisa Demuth</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota_Democratic–Farmer–Labor_Party\" title=\"Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\">Democratic (DFL)</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Ben Schierer</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Ryan Wilson</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Minnesota\" title=\"Governor of Minnesota\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Walz\" title=\"Tim Walz\">Tim Walz</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota_Democratic–Farmer–Labor_Party\" title=\"Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\">Democratic (DFL)</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1936\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDCo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Minnesota gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1937\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1936\" id=\"mwDCs\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minnesota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Minnesota gubernatorial election\">2026 Minnesota gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDCw\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Walz\" title=\"Tim Walz\" id=\"mwDC0\">Tim Walz</a>, a Democrat, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Minnesota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Minnesota gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDC4\">2022</a> with 52.3% of the vote. He initially announced a campaign for a third term, but later withdrew his candidacy in January 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt1948\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Walz26_2-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Walz26\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Walz26-2\" id=\"mwDC8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDE\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDI\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota\" title=\"Minnesota\" id=\"mwDDM\">Minnesota</a> does not have gubernatorial term limits in its <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota_Constitution\" title=\"Minnesota Constitution\" id=\"mwDDQ\">Constitution</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1951\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Walz_200-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Walz\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Walz-200\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Walz-200\" id=\"mwDDU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDc\">[</span>190<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDg\">]</span></span></a></sup> Since the adoption of four-year terms in 1962,<sup about=\"#mwt1938\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-202\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-202\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"via Constitutional referendum in 1958&lt;ref>{{cite web |title=1957 Session Laws |url=https://www.revisor.mn.gov/laws/1957/0/Session+Law/Chapter/813/pdf/ |website=Office of the Revisor of Statutes |access-date=July 24, 2024 |archive-date=August 14, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240814190758/https://www.revisor.mn.gov/laws/1957/0/Session+Law/Chapter/813/pdf/ |url-status=live }}&lt;/ref>\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a href=\"#cite_note-202\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDDk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDs\">[</span>k<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDw\">]</span></span></a></sup> no Minnesota governor has won a third term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDD0\">Following Walz's announcement of not seeking re-election, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Senate\" title=\"United States Senate\" id=\"mwDD4\">U.S. Senator</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Klobuchar\" title=\"Amy Klobuchar\" id=\"mwDD8\">Amy Klobuchar</a> announced a campaign on January 29, 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt1954\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Klobuchar_51-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Klobuchar\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Klobuchar-51\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Klobuchar-51\" id=\"mwDEA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDEE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEI\">[</span>47<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEM\">]</span></span></a></sup> Several other <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minnesota_Democratic–Farmer–Labor_Party\" title=\"Minnesota Democratic–Farmer–Labor Party\" id=\"mwDEQ\">Democratic-Farmer-Labor</a> (DFL) candidates filed, none of whom have previously held elected offices in the state. Community organizer Kobey Layne positioned herself as the Progressive candidate and challenged Klobuchar for the DFL's endorsement, but Klobuchar was endorsed in the first ballot alongside her running mate <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Schierer\" title=\"Ben Schierer\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDEU\">Ben Schierer</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1957\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-LayneMN_203-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"LayneMN\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-LayneMN-203\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-LayneMN-203\" id=\"mwDEY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDEc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEg\">[</span>192<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEk\">]</span></span></a></sup> Klobuchar would then go on to win the Democratic nomination on August 11.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDEo\">Republican candidates included State House Speaker <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisa_Demuth\" title=\"Lisa Demuth\" id=\"mwDEs\">Lisa Demuth</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1960\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Demuth_50-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Demuth\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Demuth-50\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Demuth-50\" id=\"mwDEw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDE0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDE4\">[</span>46<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDE8\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Pillow\" title=\"My Pillow\" id=\"mwDFA\">My Pillow</a> CEO and conservative activist <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Lindell\" title=\"Mike Lindell\" id=\"mwDFE\">Mike Lindell</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1963\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Lindell_204-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Lindell\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lindell-204\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Lindell-204\" id=\"mwDFI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDFM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFQ\">[</span>193<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFU\">]</span></span></a></sup> and healthcare technology executive Kendall Qualls.<sup about=\"#mwt1966\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Qualls_205-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Qualls\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Qualls-205\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Qualls-205\" id=\"mwDFY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDFc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFg\">[</span>194<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFk\">]</span></span></a></sup> Qualls received the Republican Party's endorsement after ten rounds of balloting.<sup about=\"#mwt1969\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-206\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-206\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-206\" id=\"mwDFo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDFs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFw\">[</span>195<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDF0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Demuth would go on to win the Republican nomination, defeating both Lindell and Qualls.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1970\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDF4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"32\" id=\"mwDF8\" aria-labelledby=\"Nebraska\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Nebraska\">Nebraska</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32\" title=\"Edit section: Nebraska\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1971\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDGA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Nebraska gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Nebraska\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Nebraska gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Nebraska gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Jim Pillen SelectUSA (55251574792).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jim Pillen]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Joe Kelly (Nebraska politician)|Joe Kelly]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Lynne Walz]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Ben Steffen\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image4\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee4\":{\"wt\":\"Rick Beard\"},\"party4\":{\"wt\":\"Legal Marijuana Now Party\"},\"running_mate4\":{\"wt\":\"Keenya Barnes\"},\"popular_vote4\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage4\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image5\":{\"wt\":\"Brett Lindstrom (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee5\":{\"wt\":\"[[Brett Lindstrom]]\"},\"party5\":{\"wt\":\"America First Party (Nebraska)\"},\"running_mate5\":{\"wt\":\"Mike Picard\"},\"popular_vote5\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage5\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"200px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Nebraska|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jim Pillen]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1972\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1973\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1974\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1971\" id=\"mwDGE\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Nebraska gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nebraska.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Flag_of_Nebraska.svg/60px-Flag_of_Nebraska.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Flag_of_Nebraska.svg/120px-Flag_of_Nebraska.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"30\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Nebraska_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Nebraska gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_(55251574792).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_(55251574792).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_%2855251574792%29.jpg/120px-Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_%2855251574792%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_%2855251574792%29.jpg/250px-Jim_Pillen_SelectUSA_%2855251574792%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1447\" data-file-height=\"1930\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Pillen\" title=\"Jim Pillen\">Jim Pillen</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynne_Walz\" title=\"Lynne Walz\">Lynne Walz</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Kelly_(Nebraska_politician)\" title=\"Joe Kelly (Nebraska politician)\">Joe Kelly</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Ben Steffen</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\"><hr/></td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #50C878;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #122A58;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Brett_Lindstrom_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Brett_Lindstrom_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Brett_Lindstrom_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Brett_Lindstrom_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Brett_Lindstrom_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Brett_Lindstrom_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3294\" data-file-height=\"4390\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Rick Beard</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brett_Lindstrom\" title=\"Brett Lindstrom\">Brett Lindstrom</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legal_Marijuana_Now_Party\" title=\"Legal Marijuana Now Party\">Legal Marijuana Now</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America_First_Party_(Nebraska)\" title=\"America First Party (Nebraska)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">America First</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Keenya Barnes</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Mike Picard</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Nebraska\" title=\"Governor of Nebraska\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Pillen\" title=\"Jim Pillen\">Jim Pillen</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1975\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDGI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Nebraska gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1976\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1975\" id=\"mwDGM\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nebraska_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Nebraska gubernatorial election\">2026 Nebraska gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDGQ\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Pillen\" title=\"Jim Pillen\" id=\"mwDGU\">Jim Pillen</a>, a Republican, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Nebraska_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Nebraska gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDGY\">2022</a> with 59.7% of the vote. He is running for re-election to a second term.<sup about=\"#mwt1979\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-PillenNE_207-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"PillenNE\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-PillenNE-207\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-PillenNE-207\" id=\"mwDGc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDGg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDGk\">[</span>196<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDGo\">]</span></span></a></sup> He faced some challenges in the Republican primary, including medicinal cannabis activist Jacy Todd.<sup about=\"#mwt1982\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JacyTodd_208-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JacyTodd\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JacyTodd-208\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JacyTodd-208\" id=\"mwDGs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDGw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDG0\">[</span>197<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDG4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDG8\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nebraska_Legislature\" title=\"Nebraska Legislature\" id=\"mwDHA\">state senator</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Nebraska_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Nebraska gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDHE\">2018</a> Democratic nominee for lieutenant governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynne_Walz\" title=\"Lynne Walz\" id=\"mwDHI\">Lynne Walz</a> is the Democratic nominee.<sup about=\"#mwt1985\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-WalzNE_209-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"WalzNE\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WalzNE-209\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-WalzNE-209\" id=\"mwDHM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDHQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDHU\">[</span>198<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDHY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt1986\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDHc\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"33\" id=\"mwDHg\" aria-labelledby=\"Nevada\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Nevada\">Nevada</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33\" title=\"Edit section: Nevada\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1987\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDHk\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Nevada gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Nevada\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Nevada gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Nevada gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Joe Lombardo (55512471876) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Joe Lombardo]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Nevada Attorney General Aaron Ford addresses the United Nations Human Rights Committee, October 17-18, 2023 1 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Aaron Ford (Nevada politician)|Aaron Ford]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"200px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Nevada|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Joe Lombardo]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt1988\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt1989\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt1990\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt1987\" id=\"mwDHo\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Nevada gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nevada.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Flag_of_Nevada.svg/60px-Flag_of_Nevada.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Flag_of_Nevada.svg/120px-Flag_of_Nevada.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"600\" data-file-height=\"400\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Nevada_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Nevada gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Joe_Lombardo_(55512471876)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Joe_Lombardo_(55512471876)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Joe_Lombardo_%2855512471876%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Joe_Lombardo_%2855512471876%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Joe_Lombardo_%2855512471876%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Joe_Lombardo_%2855512471876%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"959\" data-file-height=\"1278\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee,_October_17-18,_2023_1_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee,_October_17-18,_2023_1_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee%2C_October_17-18%2C_2023_1_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee%2C_October_17-18%2C_2023_1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee%2C_October_17-18%2C_2023_1_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Nevada_Attorney_General_Aaron_Ford_addresses_the_United_Nations_Human_Rights_Committee%2C_October_17-18%2C_2023_1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"549\" data-file-height=\"769\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"107\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo\" title=\"Joe Lombardo\">Joe Lombardo</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Ford_(Nevada_politician)\" title=\"Aaron Ford (Nevada politician)\">Aaron Ford</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Nevada\" title=\"Governor of Nevada\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo\" title=\"Joe Lombardo\">Joe Lombardo</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1991\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDHs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Nevada gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1992\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1991\" id=\"mwDHw\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nevada_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Nevada gubernatorial election\">2026 Nevada gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1993\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDH0\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Nevada lieutenant gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1994\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1993\" id=\"mwDH4\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nevada_lieutenant_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Nevada lieutenant gubernatorial election\">2026 Nevada lieutenant gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwDH8\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Lombardo\" title=\"Joe Lombardo\" id=\"mwDIA\">Joe Lombardo</a>, a Republican, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Nevada_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Nevada gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDIE\">2022</a> with 48.8% of the vote and is running for re-election to a second term in office.<sup about=\"#mwt1997\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Lombardo_210-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Lombardo\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lombardo-210\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Lombardo-210\" id=\"mwDII\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDIM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIQ\">[</span>199<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Businesswoman Irina Hansen, who ran for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_of_Las_Vegas\" title=\"Mayor of Las Vegas\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDIY\">Mayor of Las Vegas</a> in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Las_Vegas_mayoral_election\" title=\"2024 Las Vegas mayoral election\" id=\"mwDIc\">2024</a>, challenged Lombardo in the GOP primary.<sup about=\"#mwt2000\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HansenNV_211-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"HansenNV\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HansenNV-211\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-HansenNV-211\" id=\"mwDIg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDIk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIo\">[</span>200<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIs\">]</span></span></a></sup> Lombardo easily defeated Hansen with over 90% of the vote on June 9 and became the Republican nominee.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDIw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevada_Attorney_General\" title=\"Nevada Attorney General\" id=\"mwDI0\">State attorney general</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_D._Ford\" title=\"Aaron D. Ford\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDI4\">Aaron D. Ford</a> defeated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washoe_County,_Nevada\" title=\"Washoe County, Nevada\" id=\"mwDI8\">Washoe County</a> Commissioner <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexis_Hill_(Nevada_politician)\" title=\"Alexis Hill (Nevada politician)\" id=\"mwDJA\">Alexis Hill</a> for the Democratic nomination.<sup about=\"#mwt2003\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FordNV_212-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"FordNV\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FordNV-212\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-FordNV-212\" id=\"mwDJE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDJI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJM\">[</span>201<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2006\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-213\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-213\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-213\" id=\"mwDJU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDJY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJc\">[</span>202<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2007\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDJk\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"34\" id=\"mwDJo\" aria-labelledby=\"New_Hampshire\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"New_Hampshire\">New Hampshire</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=34\" title=\"Edit section: New Hampshire\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2008\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDJs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New Hampshire gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New Hampshire\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2024 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2024\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2028 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"2028\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"NH Governor Kelly Ayotte (December 11, 2025).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kelly Ayotte]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Cinde Warmington]]\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of New Hampshire|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kelly Ayotte]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"party3\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"candidate3\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image3\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2009\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2010\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2011\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2008\" id=\"mwDJw\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Hampshire gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Hampshire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"660\" data-file-height=\"440\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_New_Hampshire_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2024 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\">2024</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2028_New_Hampshire_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2028 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\" class=\"mw-redirect\">2028</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_(December_11,_2025).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_(December_11,_2025).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_%28December_11%2C_2025%29.jpg/120px-NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_%28December_11%2C_2025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_%28December_11%2C_2025%29.jpg/250px-NH_Governor_Kelly_Ayotte_%28December_11%2C_2025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1394\" data-file-height=\"1893\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"110\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte\" title=\"Kelly Ayotte\">Kelly Ayotte</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinde_Warmington\" title=\"Cinde Warmington\">Cinde Warmington</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_New_Hampshire\" title=\"Governor of New Hampshire\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte\" title=\"Kelly Ayotte\">Kelly Ayotte</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2012\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDJ0\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2013\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2012\" id=\"mwDJ4\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_New_Hampshire_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\">2026 New Hampshire gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDJ8\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelly_Ayotte\" title=\"Kelly Ayotte\" id=\"mwDKA\">Kelly Ayotte</a>, a Republican, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_New_Hampshire_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2024 New Hampshire gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDKE\">2024</a> with 53.6% of the vote. She won renomination for a second two-year term in 2026. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDKI\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executive_Council_of_New_Hampshire\" title=\"Executive Council of New Hampshire\" id=\"mwDKM\">executive councilor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinde_Warmington\" title=\"Cinde Warmington\" id=\"mwDKQ\">Cinde Warmington</a>, who unsuccessfully sought the Democratic nomination in 2024, won the Democratic nomination.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDKU\">Businessman Jon Kiper is running as the nominee of the newly formed Community First party.<sup about=\"#mwt2014\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-KiperCF_56-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"KiperCF\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-KiperCF-56\" id=\"mwDKY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDKc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDKg\">[</span>52<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDKk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2015\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDKo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"35\" id=\"mwDKs\" aria-labelledby=\"New_Mexico\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"New_Mexico\">New Mexico</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=35\" title=\"Edit section: New Mexico\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2016\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDKw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New Mexico gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New Mexico\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 New Mexico gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 New Mexico gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Secretary Deb Haaland, official headshot.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Deb Haaland]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stephanie Garcia Richard]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Gregg Hull]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"[[David Gallegos]]\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of New Mexico|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Michelle Lujan Grisham]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2017\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2018\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2019\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2016\" id=\"mwDK0\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Mexico gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Mexico.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1800\" data-file-height=\"1200\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_New_Mexico_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 New Mexico gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Deb_Haaland,_official_headshot.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Deb_Haaland,_official_headshot.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Secretary_Deb_Haaland%2C_official_headshot.jpg/120px-Secretary_Deb_Haaland%2C_official_headshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Secretary_Deb_Haaland%2C_official_headshot.jpg/250px-Secretary_Deb_Haaland%2C_official_headshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1902\" data-file-height=\"2333\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"111\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deb_Haaland\" title=\"Deb Haaland\">Deb Haaland</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregg_Hull\" title=\"Gregg Hull\">Gregg Hull</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephanie_Garcia_Richard\" title=\"Stephanie Garcia Richard\">Stephanie Garcia Richard</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Gallegos\" title=\"David Gallegos\">David Gallegos</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_New_Mexico\" title=\"Governor of New Mexico\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelle_Lujan_Grisham\" title=\"Michelle Lujan Grisham\">Michelle Lujan Grisham</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2020\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDK4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 New Mexico gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2021\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2020\" id=\"mwDK8\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_New_Mexico_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 New Mexico gubernatorial election\">2026 New Mexico gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDLA\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelle_Lujan_Grisham\" title=\"Michelle Lujan Grisham\" id=\"mwDLE\">Michelle Lujan Grisham</a>, a Democrat, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_New_Mexico_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 New Mexico gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDLI\">2022</a> with 52.0% of the vote. She will be term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_New_Mexico\" title=\"Constitution of New Mexico\" id=\"mwDLM\">New Mexico Constitution</a> in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDLQ\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Secretary_of_the_Interior\" title=\"United States Secretary of the Interior\" id=\"mwDLU\">U.S. Secretary of the Interior</a> and U.S. Representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deb_Haaland\" title=\"Deb Haaland\" id=\"mwDLY\">Deb Haaland</a> defeated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernalillo_County,_New_Mexico\" title=\"Bernalillo County, New Mexico\" id=\"mwDLc\">Bernalillo County</a> District Attorney Sam Bregman to win the Democratic nomination on June 2.<sup about=\"#mwt2024\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Haaland_214-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Haaland\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Haaland-214\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Haaland-214\" id=\"mwDLg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDLk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDLo\">[</span>203<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDLs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2027\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Bregman_215-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Bregman\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bregman-215\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Bregman-215\" id=\"mwDLw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDL0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDL4\">[</span>204<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDL8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwDMA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_Rancho,_New_Mexico\" title=\"Rio Rancho, New Mexico\" id=\"mwDME\">Rio Rancho</a> mayor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregg_Hull\" title=\"Gregg Hull\" id=\"mwDMI\">Gregg Hull</a><sup about=\"#mwt2030\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HullNM_216-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"HullNM\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HullNM-216\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-HullNM-216\" id=\"mwDMM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDMQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMU\">[</span>205<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMY\">]</span></span></a></sup> won the Republican nomination defeating former secretary of the New Mexico Human Services Department Duke Rodriguez<sup about=\"#mwt2033\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-217\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-217\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-217\" id=\"mwDMc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDMg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMk\">[</span>206<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMo\">]</span></span></a></sup> and businessman Doug Turner.<sup about=\"#mwt2036\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-218\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-218\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-218\" id=\"mwDMs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDMw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDM0\">[</span>207<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDM4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2037\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDM8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"36\" id=\"mwDNA\" aria-labelledby=\"New_York\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"New_York\">New York</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=36\" title=\"Edit section: New York\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2038\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDNE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"New York gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"New York\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 New York gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 New York gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"World Cup Transportation and Safety (cropped) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kathy Hochul]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Adrienne Adams (politician)|Adrienne Adams]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"File:Donald J. Trump delivers remarks on the economy at Rockland Community College in Suffern, New York on Friday, May 22, 2026 - 17 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Bruce Blakeman]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Todd Hood\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of New York|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kathy Hochul]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2039\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2040\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2041\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2038\" id=\"mwDNI\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New York gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_York.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_New_York.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_York.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_New_York.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_York.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"900\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_New_York_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 New York gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-World_Cup_Transportation_and_Safety_%28cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"758\" data-file-height=\"1011\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern,_New_York_on_Friday,_May_22,_2026_-_17_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern,_New_York_on_Friday,_May_22,_2026_-_17_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern%2C_New_York_on_Friday%2C_May_22%2C_2026_-_17_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern%2C_New_York_on_Friday%2C_May_22%2C_2026_-_17_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern%2C_New_York_on_Friday%2C_May_22%2C_2026_-_17_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Donald_J._Trump_delivers_remarks_on_the_economy_at_Rockland_Community_College_in_Suffern%2C_New_York_on_Friday%2C_May_22%2C_2026_-_17_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"409\" data-file-height=\"546\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathy_Hochul\" title=\"Kathy Hochul\">Kathy Hochul</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman\" title=\"Bruce Blakeman\">Bruce Blakeman</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adrienne_Adams_(politician)\" title=\"Adrienne Adams (politician)\">Adrienne Adams</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Todd Hood</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_New_York\" title=\"Governor of New York\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathy_Hochul\" title=\"Kathy Hochul\">Kathy Hochul</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2042\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDNM\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 New York gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2043\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2042\" id=\"mwDNQ\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_New_York_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 New York gubernatorial election\">2026 New York gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDNU\">Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\" id=\"mwDNY\">Democratic</a> governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathy_Hochul\" title=\"Kathy Hochul\" id=\"mwDNc\">Kathy Hochul</a> is running for re-election to a second full term.<sup about=\"#mwt2046\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-HochulRunning_219-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"HochulRunning\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HochulRunning-219\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-HochulRunning-219\" id=\"mwDNg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDNk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDNo\">[</span>208<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDNs\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primary_elections\" title=\"Primary elections\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDNw\">Primary elections</a> took place on June 23, 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt2049\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-220\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-220\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-220\" id=\"mwDN0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDN4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDN8\">[</span>209<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDOA\">]</span></span></a></sup> The gubernatorial candidates selected their running mates, instead of having separate primaries.<sup about=\"#mwt2052\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-221\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-221\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-221\" id=\"mwDOE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDOI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDOM\">[</span>210<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDOQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwDOU\">Hochul will face Nassau County executive <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Blakeman\" title=\"Bruce Blakeman\" id=\"mwDOY\">Bruce Blakeman</a>, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\" id=\"mwDOc\">Republican</a> nominee, in the general election. After U.S. representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elise_Stefanik\" title=\"Elise Stefanik\" id=\"mwDOg\">Elise Stefanik</a> withdrew from the Republican primary in December 2025, Blakeman was endorsed by President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\" id=\"mwDOk\">Donald Trump</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2055\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-te_222-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"te\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-te-222\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-te-222\" id=\"mwDOo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDOs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDOw\">[</span>211<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDO0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Republicans have not won a statewide election in New York since <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Pataki\" title=\"George Pataki\" id=\"mwDO4\">George Pataki</a> was re-elected governor in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2002_New_York_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2002 New York gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDO8\">2002</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2058\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-223\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-223\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-223\" id=\"mwDPA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDPE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDPI\">[</span>212<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDPM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2059\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDPQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"37\" id=\"mwDPU\" aria-labelledby=\"Ohio\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Ohio\">Ohio</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=37\" title=\"Edit section: Ohio\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2060\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDPY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Ohio gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Ohio\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Ohio gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Ohio gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Vivek Ramaswamy (55241367373) (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Vivek Ramaswamy]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Rob McColley]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Amy Acton 05 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Amy Acton]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"[[David Pepper (politician)|David Pepper]]\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"200px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Ohio|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Mike DeWine]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2061\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2062\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2063\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2060\" id=\"mwDPc\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Ohio gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ohio.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Ohio.svg/60px-Flag_of_Ohio.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Flag_of_Ohio.svg/120px-Flag_of_Ohio.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"520\" data-file-height=\"320\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"31\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Ohio_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Ohio gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vivek_Ramaswamy_(55241367373)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vivek_Ramaswamy_(55241367373)_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Vivek_Ramaswamy_%2855241367373%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Vivek_Ramaswamy_%2855241367373%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Vivek_Ramaswamy_%2855241367373%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Vivek_Ramaswamy_%2855241367373%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2348\" data-file-height=\"3128\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Amy_Acton_05_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Amy_Acton_05_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Amy_Acton_05_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Amy_Acton_05_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Amy_Acton_05_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Amy_Acton_05_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"844\" data-file-height=\"1127\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vivek_Ramaswamy\" title=\"Vivek Ramaswamy\">Vivek Ramaswamy</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Acton\" title=\"Amy Acton\">Amy Acton</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rob_McColley\" title=\"Rob McColley\">Rob McColley</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Pepper_(politician)\" title=\"David Pepper (politician)\">David Pepper</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Ohio\" title=\"Governor of Ohio\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_DeWine\" title=\"Mike DeWine\">Mike DeWine</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2064\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDPg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Ohio gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2065\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2064\" id=\"mwDPk\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Ohio_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Ohio gubernatorial election\">2026 Ohio gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDPo\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_DeWine\" title=\"Mike DeWine\" id=\"mwDPs\">Mike DeWine</a>, a Republican, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Ohio_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Ohio gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDPw\">2022</a> with 62.4% of the vote. He will be term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Ohio\" title=\"Constitution of Ohio\" id=\"mwDP0\">Ohio Constitution</a> in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDP4\">On the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\" id=\"mwDP8\">Republican</a> side, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biotechnology\" title=\"Biotechnology\" id=\"mwDQA\">biotech</a> entrepreneur and former candidate for the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Republican_Party_presidential_primaries\" title=\"2024 Republican Party presidential primaries\" id=\"mwDQE\">Republican Party nomination</a> in the 2024 presidential election <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vivek_Ramaswamy\" title=\"Vivek Ramaswamy\" id=\"mwDQI\">Vivek Ramaswamy</a> has announced a campaign, which has won the support of President Trump and Vice President Vance, the latter an Ohioan.<sup about=\"#mwt2068\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Ramaswamy_224-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Ramaswamy\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ramaswamy-224\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Ramaswamy-224\" id=\"mwDQM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQU\">[</span>213<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQY\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2071\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-225\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-225\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-225\" id=\"mwDQc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQk\">[</span>214<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQo\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_Attorney_General\" title=\"Ohio Attorney General\" id=\"mwDQs\">Ohio attorney general</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Yost\" title=\"Dave Yost\" id=\"mwDQw\">Dave Yost</a>, who announced his candidacy for governor in January 2025, withdrew from the race and endorsed Ramaswamy in May 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt2074\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-226\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-226\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-226\" id=\"mwDQ0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQ4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQ8\">[</span>215<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Ramaswamy defeated automotive entrepreneur Casey Putsch in the Republican primary on May 5, 2026.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDRE\">Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_Department_of_Health\" title=\"Ohio Department of Health\" id=\"mwDRI\">Ohio Department of Health</a> Director <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Acton\" title=\"Amy Acton\" id=\"mwDRM\">Dr. Amy Acton</a> is the Democratic nominee, as no other candidate filed by the February 4, 2026 deadline.<sup about=\"#mwt2077\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-ActonOH_227-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"ActonOH\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ActonOH-227\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-ActonOH-227\" id=\"mwDRQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDRU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRY\">[</span>216<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2080\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-228\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-228\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-228\" id=\"mwDRg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDRk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRo\">[</span>217<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2081\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDRw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"38\" id=\"mwDR0\" aria-labelledby=\"Oklahoma\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Oklahoma\">Oklahoma</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=38\" title=\"Edit section: Oklahoma\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2082\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDR4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Oklahoma gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Oklahoma\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"2030\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Mike Mazzei OK Senate Headshot.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Mike Mazzei]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Cyndi Munson.jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Cyndi Munson]]\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Oklahoma|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Kevin Stitt]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2083\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2084\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2085\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2082\" id=\"mwDR8\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Oklahoma gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg/60px-Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg/120px-Flag_of_Oklahoma.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"675\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Oklahoma_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">2030<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg/120px-Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg/250px-Mike_Mazzei_OK_Senate_Headshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"343\" data-file-height=\"480\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"107\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cyndi_Munson.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cyndi_Munson.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Cyndi_Munson.jpg/120px-Cyndi_Munson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Cyndi_Munson.jpg/250px-Cyndi_Munson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3914\" data-file-height=\"4892\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Mazzei\" title=\"Mike Mazzei\">Mike Mazzei</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyndi_Munson\" title=\"Cyndi Munson\">Cyndi Munson</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Oklahoma\" title=\"Governor of Oklahoma\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Stitt\" title=\"Kevin Stitt\">Kevin Stitt</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2086\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDSA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2087\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2086\" id=\"mwDSE\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Oklahoma_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\">2026 Oklahoma gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2088\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDSI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Oklahoma lieutenant gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2089\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2088\" id=\"mwDSM\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Oklahoma_lieutenant_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Oklahoma lieutenant gubernatorial election\">2026 Oklahoma lieutenant gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwDSQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Oklahoma\" title=\"Governor of Oklahoma\" id=\"mwDSU\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Stitt\" title=\"Kevin Stitt\" id=\"mwDSY\">Kevin Stitt</a>, a Republican, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Oklahoma_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Oklahoma gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDSc\">2022</a> with 55.4% of the vote. He will be term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Oklahoma\" title=\"Constitution of Oklahoma\" id=\"mwDSg\">Oklahoma Constitution</a> in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDSk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_Attorney_General\" title=\"Oklahoma Attorney General\" id=\"mwDSo\">Attorney General</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentner_Drummond\" title=\"Gentner Drummond\" id=\"mwDSs\">Gentner Drummond</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2092\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DrummondOK_229-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DrummondOK\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DrummondOK-229\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-DrummondOK-229\" id=\"mwDSw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDS0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDS4\">[</span>218<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDS8\">]</span></span></a></sup> former Oklahoma Secretary of Budget <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Mazzei\" title=\"Mike Mazzei\" id=\"mwDTA\">Mike Mazzei</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2095\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Mazzei_230-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Mazzei\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mazzei-230\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Mazzei-230\" id=\"mwDTE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDTI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTM\">[</span>219<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> former Speaker of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Oklahoma House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDTU\">Oklahoma House of Representatives</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_McCall\" title=\"Charles McCall\" id=\"mwDTY\">Charles McCall</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2098\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-McCall_231-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"McCall\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-McCall-231\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-McCall-231\" id=\"mwDTc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDTg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTk\">[</span>220<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTo\">]</span></span></a></sup>  former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_Secretary_of_Public_Safety\" title=\"Oklahoma Secretary of Public Safety\" id=\"mwDTs\">Oklahoma Secretary of Public Safety</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chip_Keating\" title=\"Chip Keating\" id=\"mwDTw\">Chip Keating</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2101\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Keating_232-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Keating\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Keating-232\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Keating-232\" id=\"mwDT0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDT4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDT8\">[</span>221<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUA\">]</span></span></a></sup> who is the son of former governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Keating\" title=\"Frank Keating\" id=\"mwDUE\">Frank Keating</a>, and former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_Senate\" title=\"Oklahoma Senate\" id=\"mwDUI\">state senator</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jake_A._Merrick\" title=\"Jake A. Merrick\" id=\"mwDUM\">Jake A. Merrick</a><sup about=\"#mwt2104\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Merrick_233-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Merrick\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Merrick-233\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Merrick-233\" id=\"mwDUQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDUU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUY\">[</span>222<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUc\">]</span></span></a></sup> all ran for the Republican nomination. Drummond and Mazzei advanced to a runoff, which took place on August 25. Mazzei narrowly defeated Drummond with 50.3% of the vote to become the Republican nominee. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDUg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oklahoma_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Oklahoma House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDUk\">State representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyndi_Munson\" title=\"Cyndi Munson\" id=\"mwDUo\">Cyndi Munson</a><sup about=\"#mwt2107\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MunsonOK_234-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MunsonOK\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MunsonOK-234\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MunsonOK-234\" id=\"mwDUs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDUw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDU0\">[</span>223<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDU4\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated securities trader Arya Azma<sup about=\"#mwt2110\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-235\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-235\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-235\" id=\"mwDU8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDVA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDVE\">[</span>224<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDVI\">]</span></span></a></sup> for the Democratic nomination.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2111\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDVM\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"39\" id=\"mwDVQ\" aria-labelledby=\"Oregon\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Oregon\">Oregon</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=39\" title=\"Edit section: Oregon\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2112\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDVU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Oregon gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Oregon\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Oregon gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Oregon gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Tina Kotek (cropped)1.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Tina Kotek]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Christine Drazan in August 2022 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Christine Drazan]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Oregon|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Tina Kotek]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2113\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2114\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2115\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2112\" id=\"mwDVY\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Oregon gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Oregon.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Flag_of_Oregon.svg/60px-Flag_of_Oregon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Flag_of_Oregon.svg/120px-Flag_of_Oregon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"768\" data-file-height=\"512\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Oregon_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Oregon gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tina_Kotek_(cropped)1.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Tina_Kotek_(cropped)1.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Tina_Kotek_%28cropped%291.jpg/120px-Tina_Kotek_%28cropped%291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Tina_Kotek_%28cropped%291.jpg/250px-Tina_Kotek_%28cropped%291.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2393\" data-file-height=\"2937\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"111\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Christine_Drazan_in_August_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1653\" data-file-height=\"2191\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tina_Kotek\" title=\"Tina Kotek\">Tina Kotek</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christine_Drazan\" title=\"Christine Drazan\">Christine Drazan</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Oregon\" title=\"Governor of Oregon\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tina_Kotek\" title=\"Tina Kotek\">Tina Kotek</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2116\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDVc\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Oregon gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2117\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2116\" id=\"mwDVg\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Oregon_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Oregon gubernatorial election\">2026 Oregon gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDVk\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tina_Kotek\" title=\"Tina Kotek\" id=\"mwDVo\">Tina Kotek</a>, a Democrat, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Oregon_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Oregon gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDVs\">2022</a> with 47% of the vote. She is running for re-election to a second term.<sup about=\"#mwt2120\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Kotek_236-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Kotek\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Kotek-236\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Kotek-236\" id=\"mwDVw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDV0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDV4\">[</span>225<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDV8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\n<p id=\"mwDWA\">On the Republican side, former minority leader of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregon_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Oregon House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDWE\">Oregon House of Representatives</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Oregon_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Oregon gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDWI\">2022</a> nominee for governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christine_Drazan\" title=\"Christine Drazan\" id=\"mwDWM\">Christine Drazan</a> defeated a field that included former professional basketball player and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_Oregon_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2010 Oregon gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDWQ\">2010</a> nominee <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Dudley\" title=\"Chris Dudley\" id=\"mwDWU\">Chris Dudley</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregon_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Oregon House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDWY\">state representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_Diehl\" title=\"Ed Diehl\" id=\"mwDWc\">Ed Diehl</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marion_County,_Oregon\" title=\"Marion County, Oregon\" id=\"mwDWg\">Marion County</a> commissioner Danielle Bethell, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgism\" title=\"Georgism\" id=\"mwDWk\">geonomics</a> researcher Kyle Duyck, and candidate for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregon_Commissioner_of_Labor\" title=\"Oregon Commissioner of Labor\" id=\"mwDWo\">Oregon Commissioner of Labor</a> in 2022 Robert Neuman.<sup about=\"#mwt2123\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Drazan_237-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Drazan\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Drazan-237\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Drazan-237\" id=\"mwDWs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDWw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDW0\">[</span>226<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDW4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2126\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DudleyOR_238-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DudleyOR\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DudleyOR-238\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-DudleyOR-238\" id=\"mwDW8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXE\">[</span>227<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXI\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2129\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DiehlOR_239-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DiehlOR\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DiehlOR-239\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-DiehlOR-239\" id=\"mwDXM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXU\">[</span>228<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXY\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2132\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Bethell_240-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Bethell\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bethell-240\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Bethell-240\" id=\"mwDXc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXk\">[</span>229<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2133\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDXs\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"40\" id=\"mwDXw\" aria-labelledby=\"Pennsylvania\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Pennsylvania\">Pennsylvania</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40\" title=\"Edit section: Pennsylvania\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2134\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDX0\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Pennsylvania\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Josh Shapiro December 2025 B.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Josh Shapiro]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Austin Davis (politician)|Austin Davis]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Stacy Garrity, 2025 (3x4).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stacy Garrity]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Jason Richey\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"200px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Pennsylvania|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Josh Shapiro]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2135\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2136\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2137\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2134\" id=\"mwDX4\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Pennsylvania gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Pennsylvania.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Flag_of_Pennsylvania.svg/60px-Flag_of_Pennsylvania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Flag_of_Pennsylvania.svg/120px-Flag_of_Pennsylvania.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"740\" data-file-height=\"540\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"36\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Pennsylvania_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg/120px-Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg/250px-Josh_Shapiro_December_2025_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"829\" data-file-height=\"1106\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stacy_Garrity,_2025_(3x4).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stacy_Garrity,_2025_(3x4).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Stacy_Garrity%2C_2025_%283x4%29.jpg/120px-Stacy_Garrity%2C_2025_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Stacy_Garrity%2C_2025_%283x4%29.jpg/250px-Stacy_Garrity%2C_2025_%283x4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"290\" data-file-height=\"386\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"113\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro\" title=\"Josh Shapiro\">Josh Shapiro</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacy_Garrity\" title=\"Stacy Garrity\">Stacy Garrity</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Davis_(politician)\" title=\"Austin Davis (politician)\">Austin Davis</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Jason Richey</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Pennsylvania\" title=\"Governor of Pennsylvania\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro\" title=\"Josh Shapiro\">Josh Shapiro</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2138\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDX8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2139\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2138\" id=\"mwDYA\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Pennsylvania_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\">2026 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDYE\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Shapiro\" title=\"Josh Shapiro\" id=\"mwDYI\">Josh Shapiro</a>, a Democrat, was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Pennsylvania_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Pennsylvania gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDYM\">2022</a> with 56.5% of the vote. He is running for reelection to a second term and is the Democratic nominee.<sup about=\"#mwt2142\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Shapiro_241-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Shapiro\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Shapiro-241\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Shapiro-241\" id=\"mwDYQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDYU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYY\">[</span>230<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<p id=\"mwDYg\">The Republican nominee is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasurer_of_Pennsylvania\" title=\"Treasurer of Pennsylvania\" id=\"mwDYk\">Pennsylvania Treasurer</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacy_Garrity\" title=\"Stacy Garrity\" id=\"mwDYo\">Stacy Garrity</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2146\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Garrity_242-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Garrity\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Garrity-242\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Garrity-242\" id=\"mwDYs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDYw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDY0\">[</span>231<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDY4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p><div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2143\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDY8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2147\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDZA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"41\" id=\"mwDZE\" aria-labelledby=\"Rhode_Island\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Rhode_Island\">Rhode Island</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41\" title=\"Edit section: Rhode Island\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2148\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDZI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Rhode Island gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Rhode Island\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Rhode Island  gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"2030\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"File:HelenaFoulkes (cropped).jpg\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Helena Foulkes]]\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"Aaron Guckian\"},\"image3\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"party3\":{\"wt\":\"Independent politician\"},\"nominee3\":{\"wt\":\"[[Ken Block (politician)|Ken Block]]\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Rhode Island|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Dan McKee]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2149\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2150\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2151\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2148\" id=\"mwDZM\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Rhode Island gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rhode_Island.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flag_of_Rhode_Island.svg/60px-Flag_of_Rhode_Island.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flag_of_Rhode_Island.svg/120px-Flag_of_Rhode_Island.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"660\" data-file-height=\"580\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"44\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Rhode_Island_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">2030<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:HelenaFoulkes_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:HelenaFoulkes_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/HelenaFoulkes_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-HelenaFoulkes_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-file-width=\"1450\" data-file-height=\"1793\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"121\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena_Foulkes\" title=\"Helena Foulkes\">Helena Foulkes</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Aaron Guckian</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Block_(politician)\" title=\"Ken Block (politician)\">Ken Block</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Rhode_Island\" title=\"Governor of Rhode Island\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_McKee\" title=\"Dan McKee\">Dan McKee</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2152\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDZQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2153\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2152\" id=\"mwDZU\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Rhode_Island_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\">2026 Rhode Island gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2154\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDZY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Rhode Island lieutenant gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2155\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2154\" id=\"mwDZc\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Rhode_Island_lieutenant_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Rhode Island lieutenant gubernatorial election\">2026 Rhode Island lieutenant gubernatorial election</a></div>\n<p id=\"mwDZg\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_McKee\" title=\"Dan McKee\" id=\"mwDZk\">Dan McKee</a>, a Democrat, took office in 2021 following the resignation of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Raimondo\" title=\"Gina Raimondo\" id=\"mwDZo\">Gina Raimondo</a> and was elected to a full term in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Rhode_Island_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDZs\">2022</a> with 57.9% of the vote.<sup about=\"#mwt2158\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DanMcKee_243-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DanMcKee\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DanMcKee-243\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-DanMcKee-243\" id=\"mwDZw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDZ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZ4\">[</span>232<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZ8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDaA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helena_Foulkes\" title=\"Helena Foulkes\" id=\"mwDaE\">Helena Foulkes</a>, a former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CVS_Pharmacy\" title=\"CVS Pharmacy\" id=\"mwDaI\">CVS Pharmacy</a> executive, challenged McKee in a rematch of their closely contested 2022 primary.<sup about=\"#mwt2164\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Foulkes_244-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Foulkes\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Foulkes-244\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Foulkes-244\" id=\"mwDaM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDaQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDaU\">[</span>233<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDaY\">]</span></span></a></sup> Foulkes won the nomination, defeating McKee and making him the first elected governor to lose renomination since <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Hawaii_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2014 Hawaii gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDac\">2014</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2159\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-245\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Governor [[Jeff Colyer]] of Kansas, who had taken office after the resignation of [[Sam Brownback]], was defeated by [[Kris Kobach]] in the [[2018 Kansas gubernatorial election|2018]] primary election.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a href=\"#cite_note-245\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDag\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDak\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDao\">[</span>l<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDas\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDaw\">2022 lieutenant governor nominee <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Guckian\" title=\"Aaron Guckian\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDa0\">Aaron Guckian</a><sup about=\"#mwt2167\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Guckian_246-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Guckian\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Guckian-246\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Guckian-246\" id=\"mwDa4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDa8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbA\">[</span>234<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbE\">]</span></span></a></sup> defeated actress Elaine Pelino for the Republican nomination.<sup about=\"#mwt2170\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Pelino_247-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Pelino\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pelino-247\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Pelino-247\" id=\"mwDbI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDbM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbQ\">[</span>235<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Pelino subsequently requested a recount, which was approved by the Rhode Island Board of Elections. The recount did not change the outcome.<sup about=\"#mwt2174\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-248\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-248\" id=\"mwDbY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDbc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbg\">[</span>236<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2175\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDbo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"42\" id=\"mwDbs\" aria-labelledby=\"South_Carolina\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"South_Carolina\">South Carolina</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42\" title=\"Edit section: South Carolina\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2176\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDbw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"South Carolina gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"South Carolina\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 South Carolina gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 South Carolina gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Alan Wilson in August 2025.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Alan Wilson (politician)|Alan Wilson]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Mike Reichenbach (politician)|Mike Reichenbach]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Jermaine Johnson (politician)|Jermaine Johnson]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"Sam Skardon\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"200px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of South Carolina|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Henry McMaster]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2177\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2178\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2179\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2176\" id=\"mwDb0\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">South Carolina gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg/60px-Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg/120px-Flag_of_South_Carolina.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_South_Carolina_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 South Carolina gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg/120px-Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg/250px-Alan_Wilson_in_August_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"581\" data-file-height=\"777\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Wilson_(politician)\" title=\"Alan Wilson (politician)\">Alan Wilson</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jermaine_Johnson_(politician)\" title=\"Jermaine Johnson (politician)\">Jermaine Johnson</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Reichenbach_(politician)\" title=\"Mike Reichenbach (politician)\">Mike Reichenbach</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Sam Skardon</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_South_Carolina\" title=\"Governor of South Carolina\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_McMaster\" title=\"Henry McMaster\">Henry McMaster</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2180\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDb4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 South Carolina gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2181\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2180\" id=\"mwDb8\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_South_Carolina_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 South Carolina gubernatorial election\">2026 South Carolina gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDcA\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_McMaster\" title=\"Henry McMaster\" id=\"mwDcE\">Henry McMaster</a>, a Republican, was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_South_Carolina_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 South Carolina gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDcI\">2022</a> with 58.1% of the vote. He is term-limited by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_South_Carolina\" title=\"Constitution of South Carolina\" id=\"mwDcM\">South Carolina Constitution</a> in 2026 and cannot seek re-election to a third consecutive full term. </p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDcQ\">Five Republicans contested the election; state senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Kimbrell\" title=\"Josh Kimbrell\" id=\"mwDcU\">Josh Kimbrell</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2184\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Kimbrell_249-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Kimbrell\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Kimbrell-249\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Kimbrell-249\" id=\"mwDcY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDcc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDcg\">[</span>237<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDck\">]</span></span></a></sup> attorney general <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Wilson_(politician)\" title=\"Alan Wilson (politician)\" id=\"mwDco\">Alan Wilson</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2187\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Wilson_250-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Wilson\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wilson-250\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Wilson-250\" id=\"mwDcs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDcw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDc0\">[</span>238<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDc4\">]</span></span></a></sup> lieutenant governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pamela_Evette\" title=\"Pamela Evette\" id=\"mwDc8\">Pamela Evette</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2190\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Evette_251-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Evette\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Evette-251\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Evette-251\" id=\"mwDdA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDdE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdI\">[</span>239<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdM\">]</span></span></a></sup> and U.S. representatives <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Norman\" title=\"Ralph Norman\" id=\"mwDdQ\">Ralph Norman</a><sup about=\"#mwt2193\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NormanSC_252-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NormanSC\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NormanSC-252\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-NormanSC-252\" id=\"mwDdU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDdY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdc\">[</span>240<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdg\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nancy_Mace\" title=\"Nancy Mace\" id=\"mwDdk\">Nancy Mace</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2196\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Mace_253-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Mace\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mace-253\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Mace-253\" id=\"mwDdo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDds\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdw\">[</span>241<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDd0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Evette and Wilson advanced to a runoff, which took place on June 23. Wilson won the runoff and became the Republican nominee.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDd4\">On the Democratic side, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Dakota_Democratic_Party\" title=\"South Dakota Democratic Party\" id=\"mwDd8\">state representative</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jermaine_Johnson_(politician)\" title=\"Jermaine Johnson (politician)\" id=\"mwDeA\">Jermaine Johnson</a><sup about=\"#mwt2199\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-JohnsonSC_254-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"JohnsonSC\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JohnsonSC-254\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-JohnsonSC-254\" id=\"mwDeE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDeI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDeM\">[</span>242<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDeQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> is the nominee.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2200\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDeU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"43\" id=\"mwDeY\" aria-labelledby=\"South_Dakota\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"South_Dakota\">South Dakota</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43\" title=\"Edit section: South Dakota\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2201\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDec\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"South Dakota gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"South Dakota\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 South Dakota gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 South Dakota gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"125x136px\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Larry Rhoden 2025 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Larry Rhoden]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Tony Venhuizen]]\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"3x4.svg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Dan Ahlers]]\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"[[Steven McCleerey]]\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of South Dakota|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Larry Rhoden]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2202\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2203\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2204\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" about=\"#mwt2201\" id=\"mwDeg\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">South Dakota gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Dakota.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_South_Dakota.svg/60px-Flag_of_South_Dakota.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Flag_of_South_Dakota.svg/120px-Flag_of_South_Dakota.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"720\" data-file-height=\"450\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"31\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_South_Dakota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 South Dakota gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><i>2030</i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Larry_Rhoden_2025_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Larry_Rhoden_2025_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Larry_Rhoden_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2014\" data-file-height=\"2867\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"136\" width=\"95\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"136\" width=\"102\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden\" title=\"Larry Rhoden\">Larry Rhoden</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers\" title=\"Dan Ahlers\">Dan Ahlers</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Venhuizen\" title=\"Tony Venhuizen\">Tony Venhuizen</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steven_McCleerey\" title=\"Steven McCleerey\">Steven McCleerey</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_South_Dakota\" title=\"Governor of South Dakota\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden\" title=\"Larry Rhoden\">Larry Rhoden</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2205\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDek\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 South Dakota gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2206\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2205\" id=\"mwDeo\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_South_Dakota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 South Dakota gubernatorial election\">2026 South Dakota gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDes\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_South_Dakota\" title=\"Governor of South Dakota\" id=\"mwDew\">Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Rhoden\" title=\"Larry Rhoden\" id=\"mwDe0\">Larry Rhoden</a>, a Republican, assumed office in 2025 following the resignation of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kristi_Noem\" title=\"Kristi Noem\" id=\"mwDe4\">Kristi Noem</a> to become <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Secretary_of_Homeland_Security\" title=\"United States Secretary of Homeland Security\" id=\"mwDe8\">Secretary of Homeland Security</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt2209\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Rhoden_255-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Rhoden\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rhoden-255\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Rhoden-255\" id=\"mwDfA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDfE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfI\">[</span>243<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfM\">]</span></span></a></sup> Noem had been re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_South_Dakota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 South Dakota gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDfQ\">2022</a> with 62% of the vote. Rhoden is now running for a full term.<sup about=\"#mwt2212\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-256\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-256\" id=\"mwDfU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDfY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfc\">[</span>244<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDfk\">Challenging Rhoden in the Republican primary were Speaker of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Dakota_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"South Dakota House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDfo\">South Dakota House of Representatives</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Hansen\" title=\"Jon Hansen\" id=\"mwDfs\">Jon Hansen</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt2215\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-257\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-257\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-257\" id=\"mwDfw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDf0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDf4\">[</span>245<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDf8\">]</span></span></a></sup> U.S. Representative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusty_Johnson\" title=\"Dusty Johnson\" id=\"mwDgA\">Dusty Johnson</a><sup about=\"#mwt2218\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-dustyjohnson_258-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"dustyjohnson\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-dustyjohnson-258\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-dustyjohnson-258\" id=\"mwDgE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDgI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgM\">[</span>246<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> and real estate entrepreneur Toby Doeden.<sup about=\"#mwt2221\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Doerden_259-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Doerden\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Doerden-259\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Doerden-259\" id=\"mwDgU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDgY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgc\">[</span>247<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgg\">]</span></span></a></sup> Doeden and Rhoden advanced to a runoff, which took place on July 28. Rhoden defeated Doeden in a landslide in the runoff and became the nominee.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDgk\">On the Democratic side, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Dakota_Democratic_Party\" title=\"South Dakota Democratic Party\" id=\"mwDgo\">South Dakota Democratic Party</a> executive director <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Ahlers\" title=\"Daniel Ahlers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDgs\">Daniel Ahlers</a><sup about=\"#mwt2224\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Ahlers_260-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Ahlers\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ahlers-260\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Ahlers-260\" id=\"mwDgw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDg0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDg4\">[</span>248<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDg8\">]</span></span></a></sup> is the nominee.</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2225\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDhA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"44\" id=\"mwDhE\" aria-labelledby=\"Tennessee\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Tennessee\">Tennessee</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44\" title=\"Edit section: Tennessee\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2226\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDhI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"Tennessee gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"Tennessee\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 Tennessee gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 Tennessee gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;2030&apos;&apos;\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Sen. Marsha Blackburn (R-TN) official headshot - 116th Congress (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Marsha Blackburn]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"Jerri Green (cropped).3 (cropped).jpg\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"Jerri Green\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"County results\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of Tennessee|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Bill Lee (Tennessee politician)|Bill Lee]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"Republican Party (United States)\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2227\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2228\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" ab