ion\">2022</a></div>\n<div style=\"display:table-cell; text-align:center; vertical-align:middle; padding:0 1px;width:60%;\" class=\"\"><b>November 3, 2026</b></div>\n<div style=\"display:table-cell; text-align:right; vertical-align:middle; padding:0 0 0 0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">2030<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div>\n</div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_Torres_official_portrait,_high_resolution_(1).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_Torres_official_portrait,_high_resolution_(1).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Governor_Torres_official_portrait%2C_high_resolution_%281%29.jpg/120px-Governor_Torres_official_portrait%2C_high_resolution_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Governor_Torres_official_portrait%2C_high_resolution_%281%29.jpg/250px-Governor_Torres_official_portrait%2C_high_resolution_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1295\" data-file-height=\"1728\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg/120px-BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg/250px-BJ_Attao_Headshot_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"309\" data-file-height=\"400\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"116\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:3x4.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"150\" width=\"112\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Torres\" title=\"Ralph Torres\">Ralph Torres</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blas_T._Attao\" title=\"Blas T. Attao\">Blas T. Attao</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Lawrence F. Camacho</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(Northern_Mariana_Islands)\" title=\"Republican Party (Northern Mariana Islands)\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Benjamin Jones Jr.</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Villagomez\" title=\"Edmund Villagomez\">Edmund Villagomez</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edith_DeLeon_Guerrero\" title=\"Edith DeLeon Guerrero\">Edith DeLeon Guerrero</a></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent governor</b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_M._Apatang\" title=\"David M. Apatang\">David M. Apatang</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_(United_States)\" title=\"Independent (United States)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Independent</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2386\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDxQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 Northern Mariana Islands gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2387\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2386\" id=\"mwDxU\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Northern_Mariana_Islands_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 Northern Mariana Islands gubernatorial election\">2026 Northern Mariana Islands gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDxY\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_M._Apatang\" title=\"David M. Apatang\" id=\"mwDxc\">David M. Apatang</a>, an independent, took office in 2025 upon the death of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold_Palacios\" title=\"Arnold Palacios\" id=\"mwDxg\">Arnold Palacios</a>. Palacios was elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Northern_Mariana_Islands_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Northern Mariana Islands gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDxk\">2022</a> with 54.1% of the vote. Apatang is eligible to run for a full term, but  announced on March 29, 2026, that he would not do so and instead endorsed Attao.<sup about=\"#mwt2388\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Apatang_5-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Apatang\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Apatang-5\" id=\"mwDxo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDxs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDxw\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDx0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Independent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blas_T._Attao\" title=\"Blas T. Attao\" id=\"mwDx4\">Blas T. Attao</a> and former Republican governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Torres\" title=\"Ralph Torres\" id=\"mwDx8\">Ralph Torres</a> have announced campaigns.<sup about=\"#mwt2391\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Palacios_291-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Palacios\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Palacios-291\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Palacios-291\" id=\"mwDyA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDyE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDyI\">[</span>279<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDyM\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2394\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Torres_292-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Torres\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Torres-292\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Torres-292\" id=\"mwDyQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDyU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDyY\">[</span>280<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDyc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2395\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDyg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"53\" id=\"mwDyk\" aria-labelledby=\"U.S._Virgin_Islands\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"U.S._Virgin_Islands\">U.S. Virgin Islands</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=53\" title=\"Edit section: U.S. Virgin Islands\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2396\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDyo\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Infobox election\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Infobox_election\"},\"params\":{\"election_name\":{\"wt\":\"United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\"},\"country\":{\"wt\":\"United States Virgin Islands\"},\"type\":{\"wt\":\"presidential&lt;!--DON&apos;T SET TO GUBERNATORIAL, THE INFOBOX DOESN&apos;T RECOGNIZE THAT TYPE. WE ALWAYS SET STATEWIDE ELECTIONS TO PRESIDENTIAL TYPE-->\"},\"ongoing\":{\"wt\":\"yes\"},\"turnout\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"previous_election\":{\"wt\":\"2022 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\"},\"previous_year\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"},\"next_election\":{\"wt\":\"2030 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\"},\"next_year\":{\"wt\":\"2030\"},\"election_date\":{\"wt\":\"November 3, 2026\"},\"registered\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image_size\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image1\":{\"wt\":\"Stacey Plaskett 116th Congress.jpg\"},\"nominee1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stacey Plaskett]]\"},\"running_mate1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Milton E. Potter]]\"},\"party1\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic Party (United States)\"},\"popular_vote1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage1\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"image2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"nominee2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"running_mate2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"party2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"popular_vote2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"percentage2\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_image\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"map_size\":{\"wt\":\"300px\"},\"map_caption\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"[[Governor of the United States Virgin Islands|Governor]]\"},\"before_election\":{\"wt\":\"[[Albert Bryan (politician)|Albert Bryan]]\"},\"before_party\":{\"wt\":\"[[Democratic Party of the Virgin Islands|Democratic]]\"},\"after_election\":{\"wt\":\"\"},\"after_party\":{\"wt\":\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" about=\"#mwt2397\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Infobox/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" about=\"#mwt2398\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Infobox election/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" about=\"#mwt2399\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Screen reader-only/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table vevent\" about=\"#mwt2396\" id=\"mwDys\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Flag_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands.svg/60px-Flag_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Flag_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands.svg/120px-Flag_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"\" data-file-width=\"1275\" data-file-height=\"850\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"33\" width=\"50\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></span><hr/></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%; margin:1px; display:inline-table;\">\n<div style=\"display:table-cell; text-align:left; vertical-align:middle; padding:0 0.5em 0 0;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">←</span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Virgin_Islands_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\">2022</a></div>\n<div style=\"display:table-cell; text-align:center; vertical-align:middle; padding:0 1px;width:60%;\" class=\"\"><b>November 3, 2026</b></div>\n<div style=\"display:table-cell; text-align:right; vertical-align:middle; padding:0 0 0 0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">2030<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">→</span></div>\n</div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stacey_Plaskett_116th_Congress.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Stacey_Plaskett_116th_Congress.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Stacey_Plaskett_116th_Congress.jpg/250px-Stacey_Plaskett_116th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-file-width=\"335\" data-file-height=\"410\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"150\" width=\"122\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;width:0;;\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacey_Plaskett\" title=\"Stacey Plaskett\">Stacey Plaskett</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Running<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>mate</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milton_E._Potter\" title=\"Milton E. Potter\">Milton E. Potter</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Governor of the United States Virgin Islands\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Governor</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Bryan_(politician)\" title=\"Albert Bryan (politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Albert Bryan</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_of_the_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Democratic Party of the Virgin Islands\">Democratic</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2400\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDyw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt2401\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt2400\" id=\"mwDy0\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Virgin_Islands_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2026 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\">2026 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election</a></div>\n\n<p id=\"mwDy4\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Bryan_(politician)\" title=\"Albert Bryan (politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDy8\">Albert Bryan</a> was re-elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_United_States_Virgin_Islands_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwDzA\">2022</a> with 56.1% of the vote. He will be term limited in 2026 and cannot seek re-election for a third consecutive term.<sup about=\"#mwt2404\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-293\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-293\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-293\" id=\"mwDzE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDzI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDzM\">[</span>281<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDzQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwDzU\">Current <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delegate_(United_States_Congress)\" title=\"Delegate (United States Congress)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDzY\">delegate</a> to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"United States House of Representatives\" id=\"mwDzc\">United States House of Representatives</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stacey_Plaskett\" title=\"Stacey Plaskett\" id=\"mwDzg\">Stacey Plaskett</a> defeated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lieutenant_Governor_of_the_United_States_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Lieutenant Governor of the United States Virgin Islands\" id=\"mwDzk\">Lieutenant Governor</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tregenza_Roach\" title=\"Tregenza Roach\" id=\"mwDzo\">Tregenza Roach</a> and former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legislature_of_the_Virgin_Islands\" title=\"Legislature of the Virgin Islands\" id=\"mwDzs\">senator</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donna_Frett-Gregory\" title=\"Donna Frett-Gregory\" id=\"mwDzw\">Donna Frett-Gregory</a> in the primary.<sup about=\"#mwt2407\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Frett-GregoryVI_294-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Frett-GregoryVI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Frett-GregoryVI-294\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Frett-GregoryVI-294\" id=\"mwDz0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDz4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDz8\">[</span>282<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD0A\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2410\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-295\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-295\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-295\" id=\"mwD0E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD0I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD0M\">[</span>283<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD0Q\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2413\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-RoachVI_296-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"RoachVI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-RoachVI-296\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-RoachVI-296\" id=\"mwD0U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD0Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD0c\">[</span>284<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD0g\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwD0k\">Plaskett will face Former <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Croix\" title=\"Saint Croix\" id=\"mwD0o\">Saint Croix</a> police chief and senator Oakland Benta, former Democratic senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adlah_Donastorg_Jr.\" title=\"Adlah Donastorg Jr.\" id=\"mwD0s\">Adlah Donastorg Jr.</a>, former public works commissioner Gustav James, and hedge fund executive <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_Mosler\" title=\"Warren Mosler\" id=\"mwD0w\">Warren Mosler</a>, who are running as independents in the general election.<sup about=\"#mwt2416\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-BentaVI_297-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"BentaVI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BentaVI-297\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-BentaVI-297\" id=\"mwD00\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD04\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD08\">[</span>285<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1A\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2419\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-IndependentsVI_298-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"IndependentsVI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IndependentsVI-298\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-IndependentsVI-298\" id=\"mwD1E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD1I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1M\">[</span>286<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1Q\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2422\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FrettJohnHopeVI_299-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"FrettJohnHopeVI\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FrettJohnHopeVI-299\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-FrettJohnHopeVI-299\" id=\"mwD1U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD1Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1c\">[</span>287<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1g\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt2425\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Mosler_300-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Mosler\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mosler-300\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Mosler-300\" id=\"mwD1k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD1o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1s\">[</span>288<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD1w\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt2426\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwD10\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"54\" id=\"mwD14\" aria-labelledby=\"Notes\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=54\" title=\"Edit section: Notes\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2427\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwD18\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"notelist\",\"href\":\"./Template:Notelist\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1327269900\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt2428\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Reflist/styles.css\"}}'>.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:25em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:27em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:22.5em}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-alpha]{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-roman]{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-alpha]{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-greek]{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-roman]{list-style-type:lower-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-alpha .references{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-roman .references{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-alpha .references{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-greek .references{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-roman .references{list-style-type:lower-roman}</style></span><div about=\"#mwt2427\" id=\"mwD2A\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/references\" about=\"#mwt2429\" id=\"mwD2E\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"references\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\",\"responsive\":\"1\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}'><ol class=\"mw-references references\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwD2I\"><li about=\"#cite_note-7\" id=\"cite_note-7\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"a\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD2M\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-7\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD2Q\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD2U\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Colyer\" title=\"Jeff Colyer\" id=\"mwD2Y\">Jeff Colyer</a>, who succeeded <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sam_Brownback\" title=\"Sam Brownback\" id=\"mwD2c\">Sam Brownback</a> as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_governors_of_Kansas\" title=\"List of governors of Kansas\" id=\"mwD2g\">Governor of Kansas</a> in 2017 and finished out Brownback's term, ran for a full term in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Kansas_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Kansas gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD2k\">2018</a> but lost the primary to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kris_Kobach\" title=\"Kris Kobach\" id=\"mwD2o\">Kris Kobach</a>, who lost the general election to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Kelly\" title=\"Laura Kelly\" id=\"mwD2s\">Laura Kelly</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt20\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-McKeeLoses_6-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"McKeeLoses\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-McKeeLoses-6\" id=\"mwD2w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD20\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD24\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD28\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-9\" id=\"cite_note-9\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"b\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD3A\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-9\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD3E\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD3I\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">The last elections for this group of governors, with the exception of New Hampshire and Vermont, were in 2022, except for those who became governors after their predecessor's resignation.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-17\" id=\"cite_note-17\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"c\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD3M\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-17\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD3Q\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD3U\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Ivey took office after her predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_J._Bentley\" title=\"Robert J. Bentley\" id=\"mwD3Y\">Robert J. Bentley</a>, resigned. She was subsequently elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Alabama_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Alabama gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD3c\">2018</a>.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-36\" id=\"cite_note-36\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"d\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD3g\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-36\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD3k\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD3o\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Reynolds took office after her predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terry_Branstad\" title=\"Terry Branstad\" id=\"mwD3s\">Terry Branstad</a>, resigned. She was subsequently elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Iowa_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Iowa gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD3w\">2018</a>.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-59\" id=\"cite_note-59\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"e\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD30\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-59\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD34\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD38\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Hochul took office after her predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Cuomo\" title=\"Andrew Cuomo\" id=\"mwD4A\">Andrew Cuomo</a>, resigned. She was subsequently elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_New_York_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 New York gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD4E\">2022</a>.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-68\" id=\"cite_note-68\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"f\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD4I\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-68\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD4M\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD4Q\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">McKee took office after his predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Raimondo\" title=\"Gina Raimondo\" id=\"mwD4U\">Gina Raimondo</a>, resigned. He was subsequently elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Rhode_Island_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2022 Rhode Island gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD4Y\">2022</a>.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-72\" id=\"cite_note-72\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"g\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD4c\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-72\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD4g\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD4k\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">McMaster took office after his predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikki_Haley\" title=\"Nikki Haley\" id=\"mwD4o\">Nikki Haley</a>, resigned. He was subsequently elected in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_South_Carolina_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 South Carolina gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD4s\">2018</a>.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-74\" id=\"cite_note-74\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"h\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD4w\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-74\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD40\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD44\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-74\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Rhoden took office after his predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kristi_Noem\" title=\"Kristi Noem\" id=\"mwD48\">Kristi Noem</a>, resigned.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-88\" id=\"cite_note-88\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"i\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD5A\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-88\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD5E\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD5I\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Apatang took office after his predecessor, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold_Palacios\" title=\"Arnold Palacios\" id=\"mwD5M\">Arnold Palacios</a>, died.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-89\" id=\"cite_note-89\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"j\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD5Q\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-89\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD5U\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD5Y\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-89\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Apatang's predecessor, Palacios, was elected as an independent but rejoined the Republican Party in 2024.</span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-202\" id=\"cite_note-202\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"k\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD5c\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-202\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD5g\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD5k\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-202\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">via Constitutional referendum in 1958<sup about=\"#mwt1941\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-201\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-201\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-201\" id=\"mwD5o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwD5s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD5w\">[</span>191<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwD50\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\n<li about=\"#cite_note-245\" id=\"cite_note-245\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"l\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwD54\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-245\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwD58\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwD6A\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Colyer\" title=\"Jeff Colyer\" id=\"mwD6E\">Jeff Colyer</a> of Kansas, who had taken office after the resignation of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sam_Brownback\" title=\"Sam Brownback\" id=\"mwD6I\">Sam Brownback</a>, was defeated by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kris_Kobach\" title=\"Kris Kobach\" id=\"mwD6M\">Kris Kobach</a> in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Kansas_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2018 Kansas gubernatorial election\" id=\"mwD6Q\">2018</a> primary election.</span></li>\n</ol></div></div>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"55\" id=\"mwD6U\" aria-labelledby=\"References\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"References\">References</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=55\" title=\"Edit section: References\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt2430\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwD6Y\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"reflist\",\"href\":\"./Template:Reflist\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900\" about=\"#mwt2431\" typeof=\"mw:Ext